   "text": "I read the molecule as a bifunctional (PROTAC-type) compound. It joins an imidazo[1,2-b]pyridazine kinase-inhibitor fragment to a VHL-type hydroxyproline ligand through a piperazine glutaramide linker.\n\n**Fragments, left to right:**\n- A 3-fluorophenyl group sits on C2 of a pyrrolidine. Its bond is hashed, and I assigned R from the CIP priorities (N > aryl C > ring CH2 > H).\n- The pyrrolidine nitrogen is bonded to C6 of the imidazo[1,2-b]pyridazine.\n- C3 of the imidazo[1,2-b]pyridazine is bonded to C2 of a pyridine, and C6 of the pyridine carries a piperazine nitrogen.\n- The other piperazine nitrogen is acylated by a five-carbon linker, C(=O)CCCC(=O), which ends in an amide NH.\n- That NH is on the \u03b1-carbon of tert-leucine. The hashed bond to NH gives the S (L) configuration.\n- The tert-leucine carbonyl is bonded to the nitrogen of a 4-hydroxyproline. The hashed bond at C2 and the wedged OH at C4 match the (2S,4R) pattern of the standard VHL ligand.\n- The proline carboxamide NH is bonded to a CH2 on a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl group.\n\nI wrote the stereocentres by working out the parity from the drawing for the pyrrolidine and tert-leucine centres. For the hydroxyproline I used the known VHL-ligand SMILES pattern, which agrees with the wedges as drawn.\n\nSMILES: Fc1cccc(c1)[C@H]1CCCN1c1ccc2ncc(-c3cccc(n3)N3CCN(CC3)C(=O)CCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)NCc3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)n2n1"
